gun "BD_Railgun"
  class
    slot               = 6
    selectionorder     = 9623
    ammo               = "Cell"
    hand               = main
    name               = "Railgun"
    pickupmessage      = "Railgun"
  end
  capacity             = 5     # BD's own: RailgunAmmo Inventory.MaxAmount 5 (brutal22test6 actors/MISC/Ammo.dec)
  trailprofile         = "bd_rail"   # BD22's own, in this set's RSBDEFS -- turned up
  flashprofile         = "bd_rail"
  recoilprofile        = "rail"
  firesound            = "Railgun/Fire"
  firetics             = 43
  # BD22, measured from Brutal Doom's own DECORATE 2026-10-02: 43-tic recharge before the A_Refire at Railgun.dec:240
  fullauto             = yes
  # IT IS A RAIL, NOT A PROJECTILE (2026-10-02). Owner: "the railgun visual and sound is
  # all fucked up". It fired shotclass = RailgunProjectile and nothing else, so the one
  # thing a rail gun is for -- the beam -- was never drawn.
  #
  # BD DOES THREE THINGS ON THE SHOT (Railgun.txt:121-123) and we were doing one:
  #   A_FireCustomMissile("RailgunTrailEffectMissile")   the trail
  #   A_FireCustomMissile("RailgunProjectile")           a 400-damage THRUACTORS blast
  #   A_RailAttack(400, 0, 0, "none", "none", RGF_FULLBRIGHT, 1, "RailgunPuff2")
  # The A_RailAttack is the visible rail and it was the one missing.
  #
  # shotrail REPLACES shotclass -- weapon.zs:1189-1204 skips it -- and it takes
  # its damage from shotdamage rather than from the projectile's own -- unset, ShotText
  # reports "100 (unset)" -- so BD's 400 is stated here. Flat, because BD's is
  # Damage (random(400, 400)), which is not random at all.
  #
  # NOTHING IN THE TREE SET shotrail BEFORE THIS. The capability, its colours and the
  # RS_Ballistics trail hand-off were all built and no gun had ever switched it on.
  # trailprofile = "rail" above now does something: with it set, the engine's own rail
  # colours go off and RS_Ballistics lays the profile from the muzzle to where the rail
  # actually ENDED, scatter included.
  shotrail             = yes
  shotdamage           = 400, 400     # BD's own: Damage (random(400, 400)), Railgun.txt:383
  # THE OTHER TWO OF BD'S THREE, which is where the "ass" look came from. Checked against
  # Railgun.dec tonight, and the important line is BD's OWN RailAttack:
  #
  #     A_RailAttack(400, 0, 0, "none", "none", RGF_FULLBRIGHT, 1, "RailgunPuff2")
  #
  # "none", "none" -- BD DRAWS NO ENGINE RAIL AT ALL. The whole visible shot is
  # RailgunTrailEffectMissile, a Speed 999 ripper carrying damage (random(0, 0)) that lays a
  # RailgunTrailEffect every tic down the line and, where it stops, makes BD's craters,
  # splash, flare and explosion particles. So the beam we switched on tonight was never the
  # one this gun is supposed to have; this is.
  #
  # RailgunProjectile rides with it: a slow (Speed 80) 400-damage THRUACTORS orb that bounces
  # three times and carries +FORCERADIUSDMG and a WhiteShockwave. It is a real second hit, not
  # a decoration -- the set is now BD-accurate at 400 rail PLUS a 400 bouncing blast, which is
  # what Brutal Doom does. Drop this one name if that is too much; the trail missile is the
  # look and the orb is the damage, and they are separable.
  # ONLY THE TRAIL MISSILE. BD also fires RailgunProjectile beside it (Railgun.dec:211) and
  # that is cut on the owner's call, in the headset, 2026-10-02: a Speed 80 projectile is slow
  # enough to stand and watch drift away, which reads as nonsense next to an instant beam.
  # On a flatscreen it is a detail behind the hitscan; in VR it is the thing your eye follows.
  #
  # AND MY DESCRIPTION OF IT WAS WRONG when I wired it. I read +BounceOnWalls, BounceCount 3
  # and BounceFactor 1.0 and called it a bouncing orb. The bounce STATES three lines below
  # spawn a RailgunPenetrator and `Goto Death` -- it dies on first contact and the flags exist
  # only to punch a round through to the other side. Flags named a behaviour the states did
  # not implement, and I reported the flags.
  muzzlethrow          = "RailgunTrailEffectMissile"
end

gun "BD_Rifle"
  class
    slot               = 4
    selectionorder     = 9624
    ammo               = "Clip"
    hand               = main
    name               = "Rifle"
